*{{Cite web |last=Haverford |first=Joey |date=2024-11-25 |title=The 21 Biggest Draft Steals In NBA History |url=https://www.thesportster.com/nba-biggest-draft-steals-history-nikola-jokic-kobe-bryant/ |website=TheSportster.com |access-date=April 10, 2025 |archive-date=July 25, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250725172934/https://www.thesportster.com/nba-biggest-draft-steals-history-nikola-jokic-kobe-bryant/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Jokić is an eight-time [[NBA All-Star]], eight-time [[All-NBA Team]] member (including six first-team selections) and a three-time [[NBA Most Valuable Player Award|NBA Most Valuable Player]] (MVP). He represents the [[Serbia men's national basketball team|Serbian national team]], with which he won a silver medal at the [[Basketball at the 2016 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2016 Summer Olympics]], and a bronze medal at the [[Basketball at the 2024 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2024 Summer Olympics]].

Jokić was selected 41st overall by the Nuggets in the second round of the [[2014 NBA draft]]. In the [[2020–21 NBA season|2020-21]] and [[2021–22 NBA season|2021-22]] seasons Jokić was awarded back to back [[NBA Most Valuable Player Award|NBA Most Valuable Player Awards]]. In the [[2022–23 NBA season|2022-23 season]] he finished second in MVP voting and was awarded [[NBA Finals Most Valuable Player Award|NBA Finals MVP]] after leading the Nuggets to their first-ever [[2023 NBA Finals|NBA championship]]. The following season Jokić won his third [[NBA Most Valuable Player Award]]. In the [[2024–25 NBA season|2024-25 season]] he finished second in MVP voting while averaging a triple-double with 29.6 points, 12.7 rebounds and 10.2 assists per game. The following season he averaged a triple-double for a second time with 27.7 points, 12.9 rebounds and 10.7 assists per game and finished second in MVP voting again. That season Jokić also became the only player in NBA history to lead the NBA in rebounds and assists per game in a single season.<ref>https://www.nba.com/news/nuggets-nikola-jokic-averages-triple-double-for-season</ref><ref>https://www.nba.com/news/nikola-jokic-first-player-lead-nba-assists-rebounds</ref><ref>https://www.espn.com.au/nba/story/_/id/48551947/2026-nba-mvp-nikola-jokic-shai-gilgeous-alexander-victor-wembanyama</ref>

Jokić is only the third player in NBA history to finish top 2 in MVP voting for six straight years.<ref>https://www.nba.com/news/nikola-jokic-5th-straight-top-2-finish-kia-nba-mvp-voting</ref> He is only the third player in NBA history to average a triple-double in a season and only the second player in NBA history to average a triple-double in multiple seasons.<ref>https://www.si.com/nba/nikola-jokic-third-player-nba-history-average-triple-double-full-season</ref> Jokić is second all-time among NBA players with the [[List of NBA career triple-double leaders|most triple-doubles]] and holds the record for the fastest triple-double (achieved in 14 minutes and 33 seconds).<ref name="tdrecord3">{{Cite web |last=Redford |first=Patrick |date=February 16, 2018 |title=Well That Was A Spectacular, Historic Game From Nikola Jokic |url=https://deadspin.com/well-that-was-a-spectacular-historic-game-from-nikola-1823059918 |access-date=January 28, 2023 |website=Deadspin |language=en |archive-date=October 20, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221020030412/https://deadspin.com/well-that-was-a-spectacular-historic-game-from-nikola-1823059918 |url-status=live }}</ref> He is the only NBA player ever to achieve a 30+ points, 20+ rebounds, and 20+ assists game.<ref name=":6" /> Jokić is the lowest drafted player to win either the NBA Most Valuable Player Award or the NBA Finals Most Valuable Player Award.

