'''Nickeil Alexander-Walker''' ({{IPAc-en|n|ɪ|ˈ|k|iː|l}} {{respell|nih|KEEL}};<ref>{{cite press release |author=<!--Not stated--> |title=2023-24 start of season NBA pronunciation guide |url=https://www.nba.com/news/2023-24-start-of-season-nba-pronunciation-guide |publisher=National Basketball Association |date=October 24, 2023 |access-date=May 18, 2024 |archive-date=May 17, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240517083503/https://www.nba.com/news/2023-24-start-of-season-nba-pronunciation-guide |url-status=live }}</ref> born September 2, 1998) is a Canadian professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Atlanta Hawks]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He played [[college basketball]] for the [[Virginia Tech Hokies men's basketball|Virginia Tech Hokies]]. A versatile [[Basketball positions#Guards|guard]], Alexander-Walker was selected 17th overall by the [[Brooklyn Nets]] in the [[2019 NBA draft]] but was traded shortly afterward to the [[New Orleans Pelicans]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 7, 2019 |title=Pelicans acquire rights to Alexander-Walker, Hayes, Silva |url=https://www.nba.com/pelicans/news/pelicans-acquire-rights-alexander-walker-hayes-silva |access-date=October 18, 2025 |website=New Orleans Pelicans}}</ref> He has also played for the [[Utah Jazz]] and [[Minnesota Timberwolves]] before joining the Hawks. In 2026, Alexander-Walker became the first Canadian to win the [[NBA Most Improved Player]] award.

